From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 04:45:20 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 121/162] hjviewer: lane A's follow-ups from 1.9 waves 1-2
 (pc-code staff, E2E hooks, refused PC retry)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

TV-W6 P6 (cmui's open point): every "hjv-guest-result:pc-code" result carries "staff", whether
the answer's support grant checks out for this PC as the process that registers checks it, so
the toast can promise the mark only when the PC keeps the grant.

E2E hooks the wave notes ask of lane A's files (src/hjviewer_e2e.rs):
- TV-W6 W6-E3: --hjv-e2e-support-wait <secs> makes a support code and reads the waiting room
  in the same process, "support arrived: <PC ID>" or "none" (exit 7). It reads
  hjviewer_account::get_common("hjv-support-arrived"), which is already crate-wide, so
  support.rs and the mod.rs exports stay as they are.
- TV-W6 W6-E5: --hjv-e2e-input-probe <id> <n>, a desktop session without a password that sends n
  mouse moves while the PC waits for [수락] and n more once it is in.
- TV-W3 W3-3: --hjv-e2e-peer-option <id> <name> [<value>] writes this device's option for a peer.
- TV-W9 I1-I5: --hjv-e2e-incoming prints the service's list.
- UX-G1 A6': with HJV_E2E_ACCESS_PASSWORD the connect commands print "guest held: Y|-" after the
  ticket came and again after a screenshot, stream or probe session closed, whose end lets the
  ticket go as session_closed does (hjviewer_access::e2e_session_closed).

carryover (1.8.2 checkpoint): a PC that hbbs refused registers again after 20 s with whatever it
has (reregister, REFUSED_RETRY), before hbbs drops a connection that did not register (30 s), so
it comes back about 20 s after hbbs lets it in rather than up to a minute later.

